    "title": "2026 DC Cherry Blossoms - Washington DC Cherry Blossom Watch",
    "text": "Cherry Blossom Watch Washington, D.C. Photo by David Coleman Latest Updates Cherry Blossom Watch Update: March 30, 2026 They’re still looking lovely, but the cherry blossoms are on their way out now. There’s a lot of cherry blossom snow coming down, and green leaves are starting to come through on some trees. Cherry Blossom Watch Update: March 27, 2026 It’s not the prettiest weather at the Tidal Basin this morning. A light drizzle and heavy clouds. But the beautiful flowers make up for it. And there are some important logistical updates. Cherry Blossom Watch Update: March 20, 2026 The cherry blossoms aren’t flowering yet, but there’s plenty of pink and white poking through when you look at them up close. And the saucer magnolias are still in the process of fully opening. Cherry Blossom Watch Update: March 18, 2026 Last night’s cold temperatures did knock the saucer magnolias around, but they’re expected to bounce back. The cherry blossoms are getting closer to bloom. And warmer and calmer weather is on the way. Cherry Blossom Watch Update: March 15, 2026 Okame cherry blossoms are in full bloom; Yoshino cherry trees have reached stage 2 of 6; not much change in the saucer magnolias, and see how it looks at the Tidal Basin this morning. Cherry Blossom Watch Update: March 12, 2026 In today’s edition: Saucer magnolias almost flowering; Okame cherry blossoms flowering; Yoshino cherry blossoms reach the green bud stage; and see how it looks this rainy/sleety/snowy morning at the Tidal Basin. Planning",
